b.1.1 Company Overview (Why the Enterprise System Was Implemented) 
Company Name: Nestlé  
Nestlé, a global food and beverage company, faced challenges in managing its vast operations due to outdated and disconnected legacy systems. These inefficiencies caused difficulties in inventory tracking, supply chain management, and decision-making. To address these issues, Nestlé implemented SAP, an integrated ERP system, to unify its global operations, enhance logistics and supply chain efficiency, optimize production processes, and provide real-time access to critical business data. This transformation aimed to enable quicker market responses and improve overall operational effectiveness.  
b.2.2 Implementation Process 
Nestlé's SAP implementation followed a structured approach. First, the company conducted an internal evaluation to identify key inefficiencies in its existing systems, such as inventory management and order processing. After selecting SAP for its adaptability and scalability, Nestlé customized it to meet its operational needs. The company then migrated data from older systems and trained employees to ensure a smooth transition. Before the full deployment, rigorous testing was conducted to address any issues. Once the system went live, Nestlé closely monitored its performance and made necessary improvements to enhance functionality.  

b.e3.3 key Success Factors
Several factors contributed to the successful implementation of SAP at Nestlé. The company had a clear objective—to streamline operations and improve data-driven decision-making—which kept the project aligned with business goals. Strong project management ensured that each phase was executed effectively. Employee involvement through early training and testing helped minimize resistance to change. Nestlé also collaborated closely with SAP to customize the system and receive ongoing support. Additionally, change management strategies were effectively implemented to ensure employees adapted to the new system smoothly.  

